        "The \"father of Russian Marxism\", George Plekhanov directed most of his writings against the Russian \"populist\" movement to which he once belonged. He insisted that although, in principle, in semi-feudal societies such as the Russian, the first revolution would of necessity have to be a \"capitalist\" one.",
